### Goal Model Summary

| Goal ID | Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|-------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1     | Deliver Required Resources | Ensure resources are delivered to the specified location. | # (Parallel) | Achieve | G1 -> G2, G3 [OR] | Collection and delivery can occur simultaneously. |
| G2     | Collect Resources | Gather required resources from storage locations. | ; (Sequential) | Perform | G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND] | Must navigate, request, and wait sequentially. |
| G3     | Deliver Resources | Transport resources to the specified location. | ; (Sequential) | Perform | G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND] | Transport and handle battery issues must follow each other. |
| G2.1   | Navigate to Storage Locations | Move to storage areas in optimal order. | - | Perform | G2 -> G2.1 [AND] | Essential first step before requesting resources. |
| G2.2   | Request Resources | Send message to storage for specific resources. | - | Perform | G2 -> G2.2 [AND] | Must occur after navigation. |
| G2.3   | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are retrieved. | - | Perform | G2 -> G2.3 [AND] | Final step in collection phase. |
| G3.1   | Transport Resources | Move resources to delivery location. | - | Perform | G3 -> G3.1 [AND] | Primary task of delivery phase. |
| G3.2   | Handle Low Battery | Return resources to checkpoint if battery is low. | - | Achieve | G3 -> G3.2 [AND] | Ensures resource safety and mission continuity. |

### Task Model Summary

| Task ID | Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|-------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storages | Move to storages in optimal order. | G2.1 -> AT1 [AND] | Storage Area | [1, n] | Multiple robots can collect from different storages. |
| AT2     | Send Resource Request | Message storage for resources. | G2.2 -> AT2 [AND] | Communication Channel | 1 | Single robot per request. |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are ready. | G2.3 -> AT3 [AND] | Storage Area | 1 | Each robot waits individually. |
| AT4     | Transport Resources | Move resources to delivery location. | G3.1 -> AT4 [AND] | Delivery Path | [1, n] | Multiple robots may assist if needed. |
| AT5     | Return to Checkpoint | Return resources if battery is low. | G3.2 -> AT5 [AND] | Checkpoint | 1 | Ensures resource safety and continuity. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [OR] (Parallel)**
  - Justification: Collection and delivery can be executed in parallel by different robots to reduce mission time.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND] (Sequential)**
  - Justification: The collection process must follow a sequence: navigate, request, wait.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND] (Sequential)**
  - Justification: Delivery involves first transporting resources and then handling any battery issues that arise.

This model ensures efficient resource management with parallel execution where possible and sequential steps where necessary, handling both normal operations and contingency scenarios.
